{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/runconcurrently(_:)"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"title":"runConcurrently(_:)","externalID":"s:11WorldModule0A0V15runConcurrentlyyySayAA16ConcurrentChangeVGF","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"runConcurrently","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"([","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule16ConcurrentChangeV","text":"ConcurrentChange","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"])","kind":"text"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Concurrency.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Concurrency.swift#L264"},"roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"WorldModule"},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World"]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Runs changes at the same time, each on its own copy of the world, and keeps what each one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wrote.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/runConcurrently(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"mutating","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"runConcurrently","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"changes","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule16ConcurrentChangeV","text":"ConcurrentChange","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/ConcurrentChange"},{"text":"])","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"name":"changes","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The changes to run."}]}]}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use this method to spread independent work across the processor’s cores. Each change reads","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the world as it was before any of them ran, and writes only the types its access lists, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the result is the same as running the changes one after another in any order:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0), Health(current: 10))","","world.runConcurrently([","    ConcurrentChange(access: .reads(Velocity.self).writes(Position.self)) { world in","        world.update(Position.self, reading: Velocity.self) { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","        }","    },","    ConcurrentChange(access: .writes(Health.self)) { world in","        world.update(Health.self) { health, _ in health.current -= 1 }","    },","])","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball].x, world[Health.self, of: ball].current)","\/\/ Prints \"1.0 9\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A change sees the components and resources that other changes write as missing, so its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"access must list everything it reads. Command buffers a change queues with "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/queue(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are queued in this world in the order of "},{"code":"changes","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A change must write only the component and resource types its access lists,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and must not spawn or despawn entities. It writes relations through their "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Targets"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"components, and the hierarchy through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Targets<ChildOf>"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"style":"important","name":"Important"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"c","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"·"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"t","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"), besides the cost of the changes themselves, where "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"c"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"number of changes and "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"t"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the number of component types the world has stored."}]}],"style":"note","name":"Complexity"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No two accesses conflict, and each change writes only what its access","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lists and spawns and despawns nothing; a change that breaks this traps. In debug builds,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a change that reads a component or resource type its access doesn’t list traps too. Any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change may read ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Disabled","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Prefab","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","name":"Precondition"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Prefab":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/prefab","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Prefab","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Prefab","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Prefab","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A component that marks an entity as a template for spawning copies."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Prefab","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world","title":"World","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"World","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A collection of entities, the components they hold, and resources."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Disabled":{"type":"topic","title":"Disabled","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Disabled"}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Disabled"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Disabled","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A component that makes queries and updates skip an entity, unless they ask for it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/disabled"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World/applyQueuedCommands()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/applyQueuedCommands()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Applies every queued command buffer, in the order the buffers were queued, and empties the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"queue."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"applyQueuedCommands"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6EntityV","text":"Entity"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"title":"applyQueuedCommands()","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/applyqueuedcommands()","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World/runConcurrently(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/runconcurrently(_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/runConcurrently(_:)","title":"runConcurrently(_:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"runConcurrently","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"([","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule16ConcurrentChangeV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"ConcurrentChange"},{"kind":"text","text":"])"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Runs changes at the same time, each on its own copy of the world, and keeps what each one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wrote.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Store the state of a game or simulation as entities and components, and read and change it with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"queries, updates, and commands."}],"title":"WorldModule","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/World/queue(_:)":{"type":"topic","title":"queue(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"queue"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Commands","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule8CommandsV"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"ro